#* {{RQ:Pyle Robin Hood|chapter=Robin Hood Turns Butcher|page=48|passage="Good morrow to thee, jolly fellow," quoth Robin; "thou seemest happy this merry morn."<br>"'''Ay''', that am I," quoth the jolly Butcher; "and why should I not be so?{{nb...}}"}}
#* {{RQ:Haggard She|page=284|passage=I swear also that I will honour and will cherish thee, Kallikrates, who hast been swept by the wave of time back into my arms, '''ay''', till the very end, come it soon or late.}}

